=== P2 Feature view 0138 DriveOverviewChart (Windows) ===

Capability AVAILABLE -> not BLOCKED. WinUI 3 (Windows App SDK, Microsoft.WindowsAppSDK) + .NET 10
(dotnet 10.0.300, maui-windows workload) are installed; the new DriveOverviewChart surface compiles
into the WinUI app (TeslaSync.App, net10.0-windows10.0.19041.0) and its UI-thread-free logic is
verified by the headless net10.0 test suite below. The web source
(web/src/features/driving/components/drive-detail/DriveOverviewChart.tsx) is a drive-detail composed
chart (speed Area + ideal/est range dashed Lines + SOC + usable-SOC Lines on a hidden left axis, power
Line on a right axis) with a rich Mean/Max/Min legend, plus a "No telemetry data available" empty
placeholder when chartData.length <= 1. The native feature-view owns its cache-then-network drive
telemetry read (primary/explicit vehicle -> latest/explicit drive -> /drives/{driveID}/telemetry) and
therefore reproduces the full P2 state matrix: loading / loaded / empty / error / stale / offline. The
web's two recharts Y axes are reproduced on the single native cartesian surface by pre-normalizing each
metric to a 0..1 ratio (left axis = speed/range/SOC/usable-SOC joint max; right axis = power, spanning
zero) -- the same idiom as the shipped DriveTelemetryWidget. All i18n keys (driveDetail.driveChart[.aria],
driveDetail.speed, driveDetail.rangeIdeal, driveDetail.rangeEst, driveDetail.soc, driveDetail.usableSoc,
driveDetail.power, driveDetail.noChartData + common.* + driveDetail.stat.*) resolve through the P1/S10
ILocalizer facade. Telemetry: view.opened slug=DriveOverviewChart (P1/S11).

